cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal research artifact, please cite it using this metadata. See docs/V32_RELATED_WORK.md for the current prior-work attribution."
title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation V3.2"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "Greg"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0327-6528"
version: "3.2.0-research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Dirac equation
  - lattice field theory
  - Dirac-Kähler
  - Clifford algebra
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 derivation of the free linearized Dirac equation and its scoped
  Lorentz/spin-one-half and free-fermion spectral consequences from a declared
  reciprocal complex-Psi/complex-chi C19 lattice action. The chain derives the
  action variation, exact native vacuum, finite-lattice tangent, cubical
  Kähler-Dirac/Clifford root, four-component readout, mass, time and three
  transport terms, density/current bridge, spin representation, spectral
  projectors, discrete symmetries, nonrelativistic limit, and controlled
  finite-C19 remainders. It does not claim a nonlinear localized electron,
  electromagnetic coupling, an SI/MeV mass prediction, or exact finite-spacing
  four-component Dirac factorization.
